      ":question/problem": "![](images/6a/6aadabdde81795c5e4ff384c8dc0bedc42e8e41edad2399842ff062519fc0099.png)\n\nAn observer $O$ stands $270$ meters away from a launch pad $L$ to observe the launch of a miniature rocket $R$. The angle of elevation $\u03b8$ made by the observer and the rocket is increasing at a rate of $\\frac{\u03c0}{45}$ radians per second. At what rate is the rocket gaining altitude at the moment when $\u03b8 = \\frac{\u03c0}{6}$?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
