      ":question/problem": "![](images/a0/a0b873d6f6a3ab164071484151d40ec074a1a2e6212f57280e1bb517ce817573.png)\n\nAn airplane $A$ is flying horizontally at a constant height of $600m$ above the ground. The angle of elevation $\u03b8$ made by the airplane and a nearby radar station $R$ is decreasing at a rate of $0.1$ radians per second. What is the speed of the aircraft when $\u03b8 = \\frac{\u03c0}{6}$?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
